      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Multi-slot sentence frame, not a derivation from one base. The record's formation is [group noun] + の中で + [item noun] + が + いちばん + [predicate]. The ordered-step model builds one surface from a single base and cannot express the second nominal slot or the predicate slot; emitting only the group-noun + の中で fragment would misstate the pattern as complete."
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-47",
      "nuance_tags": ["comparison"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Two-slot comparison frame, not a derivation from one base. The record's formation is [A] + より + [B] + のほうが + [predicate], with the order of A and B reversible and each slot carrying its own fixed particle. One ordered chain from a single base cannot represent two independent nominal slots."
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-48",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Closed-class lexical items, not a productive derivation. なにか / なにも are built on the single interrogative なに; the narrowest base available (noun) would license 学生か / 学生も, which do not carry these meanings. The one general rule the record states, that なにも requires the predicate in the negative, is a constraint on the verb rather than a build step from a base."
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-49",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Closed-class lexical items, not a productive derivation. だれか / どこか / だれも / どこも are built on the fixed interrogatives 誰 and どこ; the narrowest base available (noun) would license the same append on any noun. The rules the record gives, that も-forms require a negative predicate and that に/で/へ precede も (どこにも), are predicate and particle-order constraints rather than build steps from a base."
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-5",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "The point is the suppletive paradigm of one lexical adjective (いい / よい), not a construction over an open word class. Every inflected form the record lists is built on the stem よ- (よくない, よかった, よくなかった, よく) while only the affirmative present keeps いい, so no step sequence starting from いい produces them. A base of i-adjective would assert a general rule that this record exists to contradict."
    },
